{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And he built.</b> From the heavy conjugation, and also from the light conjugation, like ויפן (Exodus 7:23), ויקן (Genesis 33:19)." "<b>And he brought her.</b> He intended upon awakening and seeing her that she had been brought to him as the animals were brought, and Scripture speaks of his thought; and likewise והאנשים רדפו אחריהם (Joshua 2:7). Or she was built outside the garden, and afterward was brought to him, and when he looked he knew that she had been taken from him, for one of his ribs, together with her flesh, was not there, and he sensed that other flesh had been brought in its place."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:55.219220440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}